 "doc": {
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Synergistic block of sequential steps in bacterial folate metabolism: TMP stops dihydrofolate → tetrahydrofolate; SMX inhibits PABA → dihydropteroate."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "PCP 1st line; usually started before the diagnosis is confirmed. Add a glucocorticoid if PaO2 <70 mm Hg or A-a gradient ≥35 mm Hg. Prophylaxis: HIV with prior PCP or low CD4+ count, and many at-risk patients without HIV."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "PCP treatment:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " TMP 15–20 mg/kg/day (SMX 75–100 mg/kg/day) divided q6h for 14–21 days."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Nausea, vomiting, rash most often; more ADRs in AIDS (fever, rash, neutropenia). Serious: SJS/TEN, DRESS, hepatic necrosis, agranulocytosis/aplastic anemia: stop at the first rash. Hyperkalemia (high-dose TMP for PCP, renal insufficiency, K-raising drugs). Folate deficiency (macrocytic anemia). Benign creatinine rise (blocks tubular secretion). Hemolysis in G6PD deficiency."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Hypersensitivity to TMP or sulfonamides; prior drug-induced immune thrombocytopenia; megaloblastic anemia from folate deficiency; age <2 months; marked hepatic damage; severe renal insufficiency without monitoring; dofetilide. Pregnancy: avoid in first trimester (neural tube defects) and near term (kernicterus)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Raises warfarin effect and phenytoin, methotrexate and rifampin levels. Hyperkalemia with ACE inhibitors (case reports in elderly). PCP: avoid leucovorin (treatment failure, excess mortality)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Close K+ monitoring in at-risk patients."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Drink enough fluid to prevent crystalluria and stones."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
